 "build_recommendation": "Do not build a general offload engine (exact-prediction oracle 6.3%/1.9%, learned ~0). Optionally build E2 'verify after edit' (re-run the agent's own last learned verifier command after an edit turn; deliver 'exit 0 \u00b7 N passed' on pass, full output on fail) as an experiment: expected +1-3% $ and +0.5-1.2 calls per Haiku task, ~+1% Sonnet; confirm with a 10-pair micro-slice on click/attrs measuring p_skip (>=0.6) and harm after miss deliveries.",
 "so_what": "If shipped, verify-after-edit offload changes $/task by about -1% to -3% on Haiku (split +2.8% [2.0,3.7], LORO +1.2% [0.7,1.7]) and ~-1% on Sonnet (LORO +1.0% [0.3,1.7]), calls by -0.5 to -1.2; pass rate unmeasured offline (risk from ~1.2 unused mid-change deliveries/session). Even a perfect offload hook caps at 14.6%/9.8% of $. Confidence the realistic effect survives a live A/B: low-moderate."
